To create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS, follow these steps:

1. Create a new HTML document (you can use any text editor like Notepad, Sublime Text, or Visual Studio Code) and save it as `index.html`.

2. Add the following HTML code inside the body tag:

```html
<div id="img-container">
  <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
  <p>Caption goes here</p>
</div>
```

3. This code creates a container div with an ID of `img-container`, which will hold both the image and its caption. The image is wrapped in an anchor tag (`a`) to make it clickable, and we set its `href` attribute to the URL you want to link to. The `alt` attribute provides alternative text for the image.

4. Now let's add some styling to make our webpage look nice. Inside the head section, add the following CSS:

```css
#img-container {
  text-align: center;
}

#img-container img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

#img-container p {
  margin: 0;
  font-style: italic;
}
```

5. Save your file and open it in a web browser. You should see your image displayed with its caption below it. Click on the image to navigate to the specified URL.

