To implement bubble sort algorithm in C++ for sorting an array of integers, you can follow these steps:

1. Define a function `bubbleSort` which takes the array and its size as parameters.

2. Inside the function, loop through all the elements in the array from the first to the second-last position. In each iteration, compare adjacent elements and swap them if they are in the wrong order (the larger element is on the left).

3. Continue iterating until no swaps are made in one pass, indicating that the array is sorted.

